course: dictionary
lesson: 12252
title: Constrict: to squeeze narrower or tighter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To constrict means to make something narrower or tighter, often by squeezing it. «The snake constricted its prey» means the snake squeezed its prey tighter and tighter.
explain: Your body can constrict too. «Cold makes blood vessels constrict» means the tiny tubes in your body get narrower, which helps keep heat in. Words like narrower, squeezing and tighter are the clues that tell you the meaning.
explain: Constrict can also mean to limit what someone can do. «Tight rules constricted the players» means the rules stopped the players from moving freely. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Constrict is a verb. Its forms are constrict, constricts, constricted and constricting.
fact: «Constrict» means to make something narrower or tighter by squeezing it.
fact: In the body, blood vessels and airways constrict when they get narrower, such as in cold weather or during an asthma attack.
fact: «A constricted throat» and «constricting clothes» both show discomfort or fear, because something feels too tight.
fact: Context clues such as squeezing, narrower or limited help you work out the meaning of constrict.
exercise: «The python constricted around the rabbit.» What does constricted mean? | Stretched out long and loose | *Squeezed tighter | Ran away fast | Sang loudly
exercise: «On a cold day, blood vessels constrict to keep heat in.» What happens to blood vessels? | They disappear completely | They get wider and looser | *They get narrower | They move to the skin's surface
exercise: «Her constricting shoes made her toes ache.» What does constricting mean? | Loose and floppy | Soft and warm | Bright and shiny | *Tight and squeezing
test: «Tight rules constricted the players.» What does constricted mean here? | *Limited what the players could do | Gave the players more time to play | Moved the players to a new field | Made the players laugh
test: «During an asthma attack, the airways constrict, so breathing is hard.» What happens to the airways? | Open up to let in more air | *Get narrower | Make a loud noise | Turn into a tube of water
exam: «She felt a constricted throat when she heard the news.» What feeling does a constricted throat show? | Joy and laughter | Hunger | Sleepiness | *Fear or discomfort
